WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.688 --> 00:00:02.380
- [Narrator] Cryptocurrencies
and Wall Street

00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:03.620
have mostly been operating

00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:06.490
in two separate worlds, until now.

00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:08.640
- We are listing a stock on the Nasdaq.

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:10.500
- [Narrator] Coinbase,
the US's most popular

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:12.890
cryptocurrency exchange, is going public

00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:14.660
and that's a big deal for both Wall Street

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:16.050
and the crypto community.

00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:17.930
- Not only does it make crypto

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:19.560
and Bitcoin a little more acceptable,

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:22.566
it actually now gives
investors another way

00:00:22.566 --> 00:00:24.640
to invest in Bitcoin.

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:25.830
- [Narrator] The company allows users

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:27.960
to trade and store cryptocurrencies

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:30.030
and charges fees on all transactions.

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:32.710
It profits when cryptos
like Bitcoin trade higher

00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:34.840
and in the first quarter of 2021,

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:36.550
when Bitcoin's price doubled,

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:39.850
Coinbase's revenue was $1.8 billion.

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:42.260
Coinbase's revenue being
tied to Bitcoin's value

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:44.890
has led investors to wonder
if the platform's share price

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:46.840
will be just as volatile as Bitcoin,

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:49.070
which is known for its big price swings.

00:00:49.070 --> 00:00:51.370
Coinbase has said it wants to do much more

00:00:51.370 --> 00:00:52.560
than selling Bitcoin.

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:55.190
- We're gonna basically
try to make it easy

00:00:55.190 --> 00:00:57.110
for our customers to access
all the different things

00:00:57.110 --> 00:00:58.260
they might wanna do with crypto.

00:00:58.260 --> 00:00:59.140
- [Narrator] The crypto industry

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:01.810
has so far mostly grown
outside of the traditional

00:01:01.810 --> 00:01:03.840
and regulated investment system

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:05.980
and has an image of being a risky asset,

00:01:05.980 --> 00:01:08.120
also due to hacks and cyber crime.

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:10.360
This listing is meant
to help legitimize it.

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:11.970
So will Coinbase's public debut

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:13.603
be a turning point for crypto?

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:16.590
Nasdaq set the reference
price for Coinbase

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:19.280
at $250, which would give
the company a valuation

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:21.290
of about $65 billion.

00:01:21.290 --> 00:01:23.010
That's about eight times its valuation

00:01:23.010 --> 00:01:25.140
in a 2018 fundraising round.

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:26.230
To understand why the listing

00:01:26.230 --> 00:01:27.670
is making waves on Wall Street,

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:30.980
you have to understand what
attracted some 56 million users

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:32.140
to the platform.

00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:34.550
When Bitcoin first emerged around 2010,

00:01:34.550 --> 00:01:36.400
it wasn't exactly easy to trade.

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:38.280
WSJ crypto reporter, Paul Vigna,

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:41.530
has been following Bitcoin and
Coinbase for quite some time.

00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:43.790
- I've been writing
about Bitcoin since 2013.

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:44.632
In the early days,

00:01:44.632 --> 00:01:48.230
you had to basically download
the Bitcoin software,

00:01:48.230 --> 00:01:50.400
the actual program itself,

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:53.280
run it on your computer,
maintain a wallet,

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:55.830
maintain a node on the network

00:01:55.830 --> 00:01:57.160
and for a lot of people,

00:01:57.160 --> 00:02:00.548
it was just technologically too big a deal

00:02:00.548 --> 00:02:01.970
for them to bother with.

00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:04.140
- [Narrator] Coinbase was created in 2012

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:05.460
and was one of several platforms

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:07.560
that offered an easier
way for people to buy,

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:09.500
sell and store cryptocurrencies.

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:12.830
- The whole point of it
was to be very simple

00:02:12.830 --> 00:02:14.960
and if you look at the website, it is.

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:19.520
It is basically a very simple
way to buy and sell Bitcoin.

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:20.353
- [Narrator] The company makes money

00:02:20.353 --> 00:02:23.510
by charging a small fee when
people buy or sell crypto,

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:24.990
much like a currency exchange would

00:02:24.990 --> 00:02:27.520
if you were changing say euros to dollars.

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:29.020
And it's these transaction fees

00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:31.820
that make up the fast bulk, 96%,

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:33.450
of Coinbase's revenue

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:35.600
and what has tied the
company's performance directly

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:37.240
to those crypto markets.

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:40.990
The company made some $322
million in profit last year

00:02:40.990 --> 00:02:42.880
as crypto gained more legitimacy

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:44.650
among traditional investors.

00:02:44.650 --> 00:02:48.020
- Over the last year,
it's become hip, right?

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:51.480
Bitcoin's usage has been sort of codified.

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:52.910
That really opened the door

00:02:52.910 --> 00:02:55.030
for a lot of professional money managers,

00:02:55.030 --> 00:02:57.170
institutional money, hedge funds

00:02:57.170 --> 00:02:59.000
to come in and start playing

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:01.220
in this little exciting sandbox.

00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:03.080
- [Narrator] And then in 2021.

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:04.750
- Crypto has matured to a point

00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:05.810
where we wanted to be able

00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:07.580
to share with all investors

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:09.140
and all the public actually

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:10.287
how far the industry has come

00:03:10.287 --> 00:03:11.720
and we thought one way we could do that

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:12.730
was by going public.

00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:14.440
- [Narrator] Rather than
going public for an IPO,

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:15.780
the company has decided instead

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:17.210
to do it via a direct listing,

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:19.760
like companies like Spotify and Palantir.

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:20.930
That means that they'll save the money

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:22.610
that they would have
paid to investment banks

00:03:22.610 --> 00:03:23.740
but their shares will be sold

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:25.280
by whoever currently owns them.

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:28.161
So the company won't directly
make any money in the process.

00:03:28.161 --> 00:03:30.660
What makes Coinbase's
listing really unique

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:31.810
is that it's the first time

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:33.300
a listed company's stock performance

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:35.870
will be so closely
linked to crypto markets.

00:03:35.870 --> 00:03:39.300
- This is the first direct connection

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:42.250
between the capital markets
and the Bitcoin markets.

00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:43.083
- [Narrator] While there are some

00:03:43.083 --> 00:03:44.250
small crypto-based companies

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:46.410
that trade publicly in
the US and overseas,

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:48.840
none handles as much crypto as Coinbase,

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:52.890
which has some $223 billion
of assets on its platform.

00:03:52.890 --> 00:03:54.550
That's why its share price is expected

00:03:54.550 --> 00:03:56.480
to follow the path of its main currencies,

00:03:56.480 --> 00:03:57.830
Bitcoin and Ethereum.

00:03:57.830 --> 00:03:59.800
And that could provide
a unique opportunity

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:01.340
for traditional investors.

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:02.671
- You could almost look at the stock

00:04:02.671 --> 00:04:06.290
as an index on cryptocurrencies.

00:04:06.290 --> 00:04:08.860
If you are a mainstream stock investor

00:04:08.860 --> 00:04:12.160
and you really don't wanna
deal with Bitcoin itself,

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:14.037
you can buy Coinbase stock.

00:04:14.037 --> 00:04:19.037
It will be part of the
daily conversation now.

00:04:19.341 --> 00:04:21.120
What did Coinbase stock do today?

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:22.390
Was it up, was it down?

00:04:22.390 --> 00:04:23.740
- [Narrator] Although crypto price swings

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:26.503
can be enticing to investors
seeking high volatility,

00:04:26.503 --> 00:04:28.850
for Coinbase, having its share price tied

00:04:28.850 --> 00:04:31.810
to that fluctuating market
creates a lot of risk

00:04:31.810 --> 00:04:33.892
and may put off some investors.

00:04:33.892 --> 00:04:34.850
- If you think the Dow had a bad day,

00:04:34.850 --> 00:04:35.990
Bitcoin's was worse.

00:04:35.990 --> 00:04:37.290
- It wasn't just Bitcoin getting bashed.

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:39.556
At one point, the global
cryptocurrency market lost

00:04:39.556 --> 00:04:42.300
over $100 billion in just 24 hours.

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:45.140
- Equities going higher,
Bitcoin going lower.

00:04:45.140 --> 00:04:47.400
- [Narrator] In 2019, when
the price of Bitcoin fell,

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:49.890
Coinbase lost some $30 million.

00:04:49.890 --> 00:04:52.300
- In Coinbase's regulatory filing

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:54.480
for the direct listing,

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:57.830
they had a very long section on risk.

00:04:57.830 --> 00:05:00.179
They understand that Bitcoin
is gonna go up and down.

00:05:00.179 --> 00:05:01.930
- [Narrator] And it's not just volatility

00:05:01.930 --> 00:05:03.270
that makes Bitcoin risky.

00:05:03.270 --> 00:05:04.990
The currency has a long checkered history

00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:08.031
of being linked to cyber
crime, hacking and theft.

00:05:08.031 --> 00:05:09.050
- Coinbase has never been hacked.

00:05:09.050 --> 00:05:10.884
I have to be clear about that.

00:05:10.884 --> 00:05:12.984
That's a really big deal.

00:05:12.984 --> 00:05:14.870
But if Coinbase was ever hacked,

00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:16.640
if their security was breached,

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:19.260
if Bitcoins were ever outright stolen

00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:21.820
from the wallet that
people have on Coinbase,

00:05:21.820 --> 00:05:22.892
from their accounts,

00:05:22.892 --> 00:05:26.070
that would be a disaster for Coinbase.

00:05:26.070 --> 00:05:28.630
- We always wanna keep
cybersecurity top of mind.

00:05:28.630 --> 00:05:30.920
We've got a cyber crime
insurance policy against that

00:05:30.920 --> 00:05:32.490
but it doesn't mean that cyber security

00:05:32.490 --> 00:05:33.550
is not a big, big threat

00:05:33.550 --> 00:05:34.870
we have to keep in mind all the time.

00:05:34.870 --> 00:05:36.650
- [Narrator] To try and
distance itself from the risks

00:05:36.650 --> 00:05:38.650
of Bitcoin, Coinbase says it has built out

00:05:38.650 --> 00:05:40.520
a $1 billion war chest

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:42.830
and has started to offer
a wider range of products

00:05:42.830 --> 00:05:44.500
that it can sell to its consumers.

00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:47.410
- Coinbase, we're a retail app

00:05:47.410 --> 00:05:48.970
where people have their
primary financial account

00:05:48.970 --> 00:05:50.750
but we have an exchange underneath that,

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:51.760
we have an custodian underneath that,

00:05:51.760 --> 00:05:53.500
we have an institutional business.

00:05:53.500 --> 00:05:55.750
We also have a commerce
merchant payments business.

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:57.690
- They're prepared to
ride the ups and downs

00:05:57.690 --> 00:05:59.710
but they also wanna build a bigger boat

00:05:59.710 --> 00:06:02.110
to deal with those ups
and downs in the future.

00:06:02.110 --> 00:06:03.460
- [Narrator] Those investing in Coinbase

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:05.580
are betting that Bitcoin
will continue to grow

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:07.330
and gain more legitimacy

00:06:07.330 --> 00:06:08.740
but if the currency were to crash,

00:06:08.740 --> 00:06:10.710
as of now, that could be a big problem

00:06:10.710 --> 00:06:13.759
for the reputation of
both crypto and Coinbase.

00:06:13.759 --> 00:06:15.240
- I think it's really
important to remember

00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:19.810
that historically, Bitcoin
has gone through a few periods

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:22.080
like this where the price
has gone very, very high

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:23.410
and come crashing down.

00:06:23.410 --> 00:06:25.490
Just because Coinbase is now public,

00:06:25.490 --> 00:06:28.780
just because Bitcoin's
perception has been changed

00:06:28.780 --> 00:06:30.490
in the markets, that doesn't mean

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:33.135
that Bitcoin's never
going to go down again.

00:06:33.135 --> 00:06:35.885
(dramatic music)

